1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:11,390
Slide 4 defines "PERSISTENT CLOUD AUTONOMY: The Three Invariants of Sleep-Free Systems." James, let's break down why each of these three cards is mandatory.

2
00:00:12,290 --> 00:00:14,257
Card 1: Headless Execution.

3
00:00:14,257 --> 00:00:17,973
A lot of people think an AI needs a browser window.

4
00:00:17,973 --> 00:00:26,500
In Spark OS, our daemon runs headlessly in Python, consuming less than 120MB of RAM—lighter than a single Chrome tab!

5
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,928
Card 2: Atomic State Checkpoints.

6
00:00:29,928 --> 00:00:31,460
This is my favorite!

7
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:40,808
After every single tool call—whether querying a database or drafting an email—the agent commits its exact state to SQLite.

8
00:00:40,808 --> 00:00:46,020
Even if the underlying VM suffers a kernel panic, zero data is lost!

9
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,969
And Card 3: Proactive Sensing!

10
00:00:48,969 --> 00:00:54,093
A traditional chatbot is completely deaf and blind until you type a prompt.

11
00:00:54,093 --> 00:01:01,610
Our Spark guardian actively listens to Gmail webhooks, Calendar reminders, and database events 24 hours a day!

12
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:10,650
So when an urgent customer email hits the server at 3:15 AM, the agent senses it instantly and begins triage immediately!

13
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:21,340
When Headless Execution, Atomic Checkpoints, and Proactive Sensing unite, your agent becomes a living, vigilant sentry in cyberspace.

